A||||7||batboy||striking it rich with Fieros||||1
Z||000000||batboy||09-18-1999||12:43 PM||||Last time I was in a salvage yard looking for parts, I found a roach (not the insect) and 63 cents in change behind the seat of one wrecked Fiero. When I bought the Batmobile I found some little screws and loose change in one of the ashtrays, plus a pair of cheap sunglasses and several maps under the seat. I just had the console apart on my GT and found $2.12 that was rattling around in there. So, I then went to my ol' 1987 2.5 Fiero (which has a dead engine right now) and after searching around in it I found a quarter. Hmmmm, seems like these Fieros are a gold mine for lost coins and maybe a few other misc. things.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||09-18-1999||08:07 PM||||A friend of mine imported a Corvette from Miami. He didn't find any loose change. He did however found a few bullets!||||reg||10
Z||000002||yellowFormula||09-19-1999||12:40 AM||||Yeah I know what you mean Batboy, when I bought my Formula I was vaccuming it out and I moved the seat up to find around 3 or 4 dollaris in change, the passenger had about 2 dollars in change, and the map pockets had about a dollar in each. Then I looked in my Coupes and I found change behind/under the seats also, my theory is it's all in the way you seat, the Fiero sits low and you kinda sit back a little, and with men's pants, change will fall out when your driving and you don't even realize it.||||reg||10
Z||000003||batboy||09-19-1999||09:40 AM||||I went to the auto boneyard yesterday and found a handful of little parts I needed for two of my Fieros. I started poking around in junk cars, behind and under the seats, and found enough loose change to pay for the parts I was buying! I thought that was funny. I could barely keep a straight face when I was paying the salvage yard guy.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bruce||09-19-1999||09:34 PM||||they say that's how Rockerfeller got started.||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||09-20-1999||07:22 AM||||A friend told me once that that it was surprising that I didn't squeak when I walked because I was so tight with my money.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||09-20-1999||08:26 AM||||Three of the Fieros I have all had Haynes Manuals behind the seats......<P>Sometimes thats a good thing, sometimes its not........||||reg||1
